<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Brierley ups Coles stake.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Brierley ups Coles stake.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand investment group Brierley Investment Ltd said on Monday it has raised its stake in Australia's largest retailer, Coles Myer Ltd, to 6.8 percent from 5.01 percent previously.  </p>
<p>Brierley said in a substantial shareholder notice to the Australian Stock Exchange that it now held 73.47 million Coles Myer shares, up from 53.67 million.</p>
<p>Coles Myer has about 1.08 billion shares on issue. Brierley said the Coles shares are held by the company and its Australian associate Australian Consolidated Investments Ltd.</p>
<p>Coles shares closed one cent higher at A$4.43, which values Brierley's stake at A$325.47 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
